# Copy this to .env.secrets and fill in the values. That file is gitignored
# (.env.* in .gitignore) and must never be committed.
#
#   cp .env.secrets.template .env.secrets
#   chmod 600 .env.secrets
#   ./tools/push-secrets.sh
#
# Why this file exists: Cloudflare Worker secrets are write-only. Once set, no
# command can read them back, so there is no way to tell a correct secret from a
# wrong one — or from an empty one — without exercising the thing that uses it.
# Every fault on 30-31 August 2026 was a value that looked set and was not:
# an empty relay key, a Turnstile secret from the wrong widget, a GitHub token
# GitHub refused. This file is the record; push-secrets.sh verifies each value
# against the service that owns it before sending it anywhere.
#
# Keep no blank line inside a value and no quotes around it.

# Turnstile — BOTH halves come from the SAME widget in the Cloudflare
# dashboard (Turnstile -> your widget -> Settings). They are a matched pair and
# one without the other fails with a green widget and a server refusal.
# The site key is public and lives in .env / GitHub Actions, not here.
# Verified by: siteverify must answer invalid-input-response, not
# invalid-input-secret. Roughly 35 characters.
TURNSTILE_SECRET_KEY=

# Shared bearer token between this Worker and the adnet mail relay at
# ads.oze.net.au. Both ends must hold the SAME string, compared byte for byte.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32
# push-secrets.sh sets it on lovemallacoota AND adnet-serve together, which is
# the only way to be sure they match.
RELAY_KEY=

# Fine-grained GitHub PAT, repository access limited to coldix/lovemallacoota,
# Repository permissions -> Contents: Read and write. Used to commit listing
# submissions and staged photographs. Expires — put the date in your calendar,
# because when it lapses submissions fail with a 401 that nobody sees.
# Verified by: GET /repos/coldix/lovemallacoota must return 200.
GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Transactional sending for verification codes, from resend.com. The adnet relay
# cannot do this job: it sends to one fixed address by design, and Cloudflare
# Email Routing behind it only delivers to addresses verified on the account, so
# a member of the public could never receive a code. Starts re_.
# The sending domain in MAIL_FROM (wrangler.jsonc) must be verified with Resend,
# which means adding their DNS records to lovemallacoota.au.
# Verified by: GET https://api.resend.com/domains returns 200.
RESEND_API_KEY=

# From the Stripe dashboard, the signing secret for the webhook endpoint
# pointing at https://lovemallacoota.au/api/stripe. Starts whsec_.
# Developers -> Webhooks -> that endpoint -> Signing secret -> Reveal.
# No safe read-only verification exists, so this one is pushed unchecked.
# Production already holds a working value, so a blank line here breaks
# nothing today; it means only that this record cannot rebuild production.
# push-secrets.sh says so at the top of every run until it is filled in.
STRIPE_WEBHOOK_SECRET=
